Subject: server: create --slot-save-path directory when missing

--slot-save-path rejected paths that don't exist yet, which makes it
impossible to bake the flag into a packaged llamafile's default args
(the target directory can't be pre-created on the user's machine).
Create it instead, and only error if creation also fails. The trailing
separator matters: fs_create_directory_with_parents only creates path
components that are terminated by a separator, so without it only the
parents of the requested directory would be created.

diff --git a/common/arg.cpp b/common/arg.cpp
--- a/common/arg.cpp
+++ b/common/arg.cpp
@@ -3089,7 +3089,10 @@ common_params_context common_params_parser_init(common_params & params, llama_ex
         "path to save slot kv cache (default: disabled)",
         [](common_params & params, const std::string & value) {
             params.slot_save_path = value;
-            if (!fs_is_directory(params.slot_save_path)) {
+            // note: trailing separator required — fs_create_directory_with_parents
+            // only creates components terminated by a separator
+            if (!fs_is_directory(params.slot_save_path) &&
+                !fs_create_directory_with_parents(params.slot_save_path + DIRECTORY_SEPARATOR)) {
                 throw std::invalid_argument("not a directory: " + value);
             }
             // if doesn't end with DIRECTORY_SEPARATOR, add it
